And the chances of these things occuring?  Assuming you have 30 items in
your inventory, which is probably low, that's only a 1/30 chance per
round of your BoH being hit.  The maximum chance of a spellcasting
monster choosing a curse is slightly less than 1/4.  The chance of an
intervention being a curse is 1/6 (1/4 on Astral) and interventions only
occur every 1d200+49 turns (IIRC).  

I'm not going to do the math, but even if you have two liches or other
spellcasting monsters attacking in the same round, even if we assume
they both choose to curse you, that's still just a 1/900 chance (if you
have 30 items in inventory) that they'll both hit your BoH.  In reality,
of course, the chance is significantly lower.  

Generally, a person is more likely to slip up while typing and put a
/oCanc in his or her BoH than to actually need the /oCanc to uncurse
said bag, assuming the person is even marginally prepared.  

